1
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:42,800
[She's Wild Fire]

2
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:47,760
[Episode 9:
My Feelings Have Never Changed]

3
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:57,200
Wait.

4
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,580
I'm the person you're meeting today.

5
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,960
Since when did you
start going by Wang Biao?

6
00:01:09,039 --> 00:01:09,720
Have a seat.

7
00:01:10,039 --> 00:01:12,120
Let's discuss the investment project

8
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,520
you wanted to talk about.

9
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:23,900
Here's my business proposal.

10
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:26,370
Please take a look, Mr. Chu.

11
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:31,090
[Business Proposal]

12
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:35,920
Regarding this project,

13
00:01:36,280 --> 00:01:37,039
there are a few things

14
00:01:37,039 --> 00:01:38,640
I'd like to confirm with you.

15
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:39,720
Of course.

16
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:42,039
What's the revenue model
for this project?

17
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:42,920
It's on page 12.

18
00:01:43,479 --> 00:01:46,080
There are several options
for investment and returns.

19
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,920
You can refer to whichever one

20
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,320
suits your preferences.

21
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,400
What about the timeline?

22
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:55,400
Page 19.

23
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:57,720
If you're interested, Mr. Chu,

24
00:01:57,720 --> 00:02:00,180
I'd be happy to walk you
through each option.

25
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:01,040
About the project...

26
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,970
Have you missed me all these years?

27
00:02:09,759 --> 00:02:11,490
What year did you go to America?

28
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:13,320
1991.

29
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:14,940
Which month, exactly?

30
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:16,960
Lunar or solar calendar?

31
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,730
December, solar calendar.

32
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:26,870
So while you were there,

33
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:29,130
you studied at Parsons the whole time?

34
00:02:35,079 --> 00:02:37,280
Did you meet many Chinese people there?

35
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,280
Chu Chunsheng,

36
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:40,480
don't be like this.

37
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:46,720
I just want to get to know you better.

38
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,800
After all, we're going
to be business partners.

39
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,160
It's perfectly normal

40
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,680
for us to get to know each other,

41
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,210
isn't it?

42
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,120
Actually, I have a few other questions.

43
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,000
For instance,
if we were to work together...

44
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,200
You don't need to ask.

45
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,770
It's not what you think.

46
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:16,000
And what exactly do you think I think?

47
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,600
You're not Nannan's father.

48
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,320
Who is it?

49
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:47,380
What are you doing?

50
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,079
Boss?

51
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:54,640
How'd you get in here?

52
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,100
I asked the waiter
to open the door for me.

53
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:04,360
What's so urgent that you had to
come see me in the middle of the night?

54
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:06,800
It's nothing urgent.

55
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,720
It's just...

56
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,280
A friend of mine...

57
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,760
A friend?

58
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,140
What happened?

59
00:04:17,010 --> 00:04:18,339
Trouble with business?

60
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:19,800
No, not business.

61
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:20,440
It's...

62
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:23,070
A relationship issue.

63
00:04:23,070 --> 00:04:24,330
A relationship issue?

64
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:25,920
If that's what you want to talk about,

65
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,280
I'm wide awake now.

66
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:29,140
Go on. Tell me about it.

67
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:34,680
Well...

68
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:36,840
My friend, he...

69
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,240
likes a woman.

70
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:38,920
He's

71
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:40,840
liked her for a long time.

72
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,000
But then,

73
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:43,640
the woman

74
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:44,800
just left.

75
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,720
When they met again after she came back,

76
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:48,200
she had a kid with her.

77
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,480
And the kid looks a lot like him.

78
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:51,800
Even their habits

79
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:54,720
and mannerisms are exactly the same.

80
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:57,400
But the woman insists
the kid has nothing to do with him.

81
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,400
Could you be talking about Miss Xie?

82
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,200
No.

83
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:09,120
It's the woman your friend likes.

84
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:11,320
Does she still love your friend?

85
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,480
Of course she doesn't.

86
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,120
Boss,

87
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,000
think about it.

88
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:23,880
If that woman still loved your friend,

89
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:27,640
and the kid looked
and acted so much like him...

90
00:05:27,950 --> 00:05:29,950
Are you left-handed?

91
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,880
She'd be rushing to bring the child

92
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,610
to introduce him as the father.

93
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,560
That's my private business.

94
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,200
I have no reason to tell you.

95
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,080
Mom!

96
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:41,400
Raising a child alone
is so hard for a woman.

97
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:42,800
She'd be exhausted.

98
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,600
Then suddenly, some caring,

99
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,060
loving big shot
comes along to claim his son.

100
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,000
She'd be over the moon!

101
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:54,730
Why would she hide from him and insist
the kid has nothing to do with him?

102
00:05:58,159 --> 00:05:58,800
Boss.

103
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,080
Boss?

104
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:02,080
Boss?

105
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:04,000
Boss?

106
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,120
What are you doing up so late?

107
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,340
Go to sleep.

108
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,200
So...

109
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,370
She doesn't love me.

110
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,600
Is this child mine?

111
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:45,120
You don't need to ask.

112
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,690
It's not what you think.

113
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,260
And what exactly do you think I think?

114
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,640
You're not Nannan's father.

115
00:06:55,120 --> 00:06:56,000
Dad.

116
00:06:56,050 --> 00:06:58,530
Then hurry up and win Mom back.

117
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,200
Xie Nanfeng,

118
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,520
in the past,

119
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:06,320
all we had between us was
endless suspicion and testing each other.

120
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,920
Not a single word of honesty.

121
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:11,220
I don't want things to go on like this.

122
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,690
And I don't want
to leave any more regrets.

123
00:07:13,960 --> 00:07:15,200
From now on,

124
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,020
I won't hesitate anymore.

125
00:07:17,160 --> 00:07:18,520
I'll tell you

126
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:20,600
just how much I love you.

127
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:30,250
Where do you think
the investment terms need to be adjusted?

128
00:07:30,510 --> 00:07:33,970
You're not making things difficult
for me on purpose, are you?

129
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,440
I asked you here today

130
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:57,700
because I want to finish
what I couldn't 5 years ago.

131
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:13,600
Xie Nanfeng,

132
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,920
will you marry me?

133
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,000
For the past 5 years,

134
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,600
my feelings have never changed.

135
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,480
Chu Chunsheng,

136
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,400
whether I left 5 years ago

137
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,720
or came back this time,

138
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,860
there has only ever been 1 reason.

139
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,010
And it's not you.

140
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:04,600
It's Shencheng First Garment Factory.

141
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,280
I want to win the contract

142
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:10,400
and create a brand
of our own for Shencheng,

143
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,360
one that can reach the world.

144
00:09:29,850 --> 00:09:30,490
I'm sorry.

145
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,880
Someone has already booked
the entire venue for today.

146
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:33,800
Booked the entire venue?

147
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,400
Who has that kind of pull?

148
00:09:49,920 --> 00:09:51,080
My life

149
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:54,170
holds possibilities beyond love.

150
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:56,800
Right now,

151
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:59,730
I just want to be completely myself

152
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,930
and build my career.

153
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:07,120
♪ Before the raindrops fall,
blurring the view ♪

154
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:14,150
♪ Memories replay like a silent film ♪

155
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:21,370
♪ The warmth of your fingertips
has long faded in the wind ♪

156
00:10:21,950 --> 00:10:24,370
♪ The moment you turned away ♪

157
00:10:25,420 --> 00:10:30,370
♪ Silence becomes so heavy ♪

158
00:10:31,310 --> 00:10:39,120
♪ Why meet if we are destined to part ♪

159
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:40,360
All right.

160
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:46,090
♪ Tears drown my breath ♪

161
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:43,000
I'll walk this road with you

162
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:47,600
until you reach the place
you've always dreamed of.

163
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:53,230
♪ The sound of a broken heart
in this merciless night ♪

164
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:52,280
When you reach the place
you've dreamed of,

165
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:55,200
be sure to look back.

166
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:56,850
♪ Only memories remain ♪

167
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:02,430
♪ I still want to cherish it ♪

168
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:09,380
♪ Please don't leave ♪

169
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,400
Thank you.

170
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:11,000
If they get married

171
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:13,060
and Chu Chunsheng invests in her,

172
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:14,890
I'll have no chance of winning.

173
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:16,000
No.

174
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,800
I can't let them get together.
